## Why This Is Asked
Tests secure, rotating certs in Swarm with Vault, handling cert storage (secret vs volume), and canary semantics.

## Key Concepts
- Swarm multi-node with TLS and mTLS
- Vault PKI for dynamic certs
- Certs via writable volume + sidecar refresh
- Canary rollout with health checks and rollback
- Nginx TLS termination and service-to-service mTLS

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple cert refresh watcher from Vault to a mounted volume
const fetch = require('node-fetch');
const fs = require('fs');
async function refresh() {
  const res = await fetch('https://vault.example/v1/pki/issue/api', { headers: { 'X-Vault-Token': process.env.VAULT_TOKEN } });
  const cert = await res.text();
  fs.writeFileSync('/certs/api.crt', cert);
}
setInterval(refresh, 5 * 60 * 1000);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate cert rotation does not break existing connections?
- How would you monitor Vault token renewal and automatic revocation?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical knowledge of per-tenant configuration via Docker Config, feature gating, and edge proxy routing in a multi-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for per-tenant rules
- Feature flag gating in API
- Traefik TLS and docker-dca wiring
- Lightweight bootstrap and config reload

## Code Example
```javascript
// sample Express middleware for feature gate
const fs = require('fs');
let flags = {};
try { flags = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/config/feature-flags.json','utf8')); } catch(e) { flags = {}; }
function featureGate(req,res,next){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  if(!tenant) return res.status(400).send('Missing X-Tenant');
  const enabled = flags[tenant] && flags[tenant].includes('new-feature');
  if(!enabled) return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');
  next();
}
app.get('/new-feature', featureGate, (req,res)=>{ res.send('New feature access granted'); });
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you hot-reload the flags without restarting the API?
- How would you test isolation across tenants when flags change?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to wire config-driven per-tenant controls in a multi-DC docker-dca setup, with TLS edge and simple runtime enforcement.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for runtime limits
- Per-tenant rate limiting (token bucket)
- TLS via Traefik edge proxy
- Basic cross-DC deployment considerations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: token bucket per tenant with 60 rpm
const limits = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/etc/config/tenant-rate-limits.json','utf8'));
const buckets = new Map();
function allow(tenant){
  const now = Date.now();
  let b = buckets.get(tenant);
  if(!b){ b = {tokens: limits[tenant]||0, last: now}; buckets.set(tenant,b); }
  // simplistic: refill 1 token per second for 60s window
  const elapsed = (now - b.last)/1000; b.last = now; b.tokens = Math.min((limits[tenant]||0), b.tokens + elapsed);
  if(b.tokens >= 1){ b.tokens--; return true; }
  return false;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you safely refresh Docker Config without restarting all containers?
- What edge cases arise with clock skew or config changes?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a tenant-aware resilience and security workflow across DCs, combining secret management, mTLS, and controlled fault injection.

## Key Concepts
- Vault-driven per-tenant fault policies
- Nginx Lua for ingress-level fault injection
- SPIFFE SVIDs and TLS rotation per workload
- SLA-based canary/rollback and observability

## Code Example
```javascript
function getTenantPolicy(tenant) {
  // pseudo-call to Vault to fetch policy
  return vault.fetchPolicy(tenant) || { latencyMs: 0, dropRate: 0 };
}
function shouldInject(tenant) {
  const p = getTenantPolicy(tenant);
  return Math.random() < p.dropRate ? 'drop' : 'latency';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test SLA breach detection and rollback in a live cluster?
- How do you ensure policy changes are hot-applied without restarting proxies?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to drive feature-flag configurations from Docker Configs in a multi-DC setup, plus per-tenant routing and safe fallbacks.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Configs for per-tenant flags
- X-Tenant header routing and fallback strategies
- In-process caching with TTL and config-driven feature gates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js Express snippet to load tenant flags from docker config mounted at /config
app.use((req,res,next)=>{
  const t = req.header('X-Tenant');
  let flags = cache.get(t);
  if(!flags){
    try{
      const raw = fs.readFileSync(`/config/feature-flags-${t}.json`, 'utf8');
      flags = JSON.parse(raw);
      cache.set(t, flags);
    }catch(e){
      flags = globalDefaults;
    }
  }
  req.flags = flags;
  next();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you invalidate tenant flag cache when the Docker Config changes without restarting the API?
- How would you test this across two DCs with Traefik and simulate Config updates?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end trust from image provenance to runtime policy enforcement, plus canary control and rollback.

## Key Concepts
